          "update_time": 1792965739.489,
          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "Revised the manuscript to integrate Notes 54–55, reorganize the argument, and derive the new analytical results systematically. The 112-page PDF builds cleanly, with references, links and rendered pages checked.\n\n:codex-file-citation{path=\"/Users/ebbaker/Documents/shifted-zeta-positivity/output/pdf/heat_density_asymptotics/heat_density_asymptotics.pdf\" purpose=\"output\"}\n\nThe main advance is a finite construction covering **every real time and height**, on the declared transverse strip, with both endpoint comparisons and actual covariance retained. The conditioning improvement reduces the specified sufficient source-size bound from a quadratic exponential to\n\\[\n\\log S_{\\mathrm{bound}}=\\pi R/32+O(\\log^2R)\n\\]\nat fixed upper time and accuracy. The constants remain potentially prohibitive.\n\nThe [focused review](/Users/ebbaker/Documents/shifted-zeta-positivity/papers/investigations-5/01_heat_density_asymptotics/reviews/36_NOTES54_55_REVIEW_AND_INTEGRATION_20261025.md) found no blocking error in the inspected mechanisms. The full-chain audit remains outstanding; numerical diagnostics remain supporting material.\n\nThe strongest next step is **Analysis — Sol**, using [HDA-17-AN05 r1](/Users/ebbaker/Documents/shifted-zeta-positivity/papers/investigations-5/01_heat_density_asymptotics/research-progress/handoffs/HDA-17-AN05.md): prove a positive compressed-source construction with the complete four-jet and cost bounds. Evaluation precision and continuous averaging should follow as separate obligations.\n\nThe detailed assessment is saved in [the program outlook note](/Users/ebbaker/Documents/shifted-zeta-positivity/papers/investigations-5/01_heat_density_asymptotics/notes/57_PROGRAM_OUTLOOK_AFTER_ALL_TIME_CONSTRUCTION_20261025.md). Progress, milestone history and chat history were updated; final-reply capture is arranged.\n\nContinuation: “Continue HDA-17-AN05 r1 using Note57 and Review36; prove the compressed-source bound or identify its first exact unpaid analytic input.”"
            ]
